*** A1b-opdecl-arity — op-decl underscore/arity mismatch: oracle disables, tnk crashes (fable-audit.md §3.1)
*** Case 1: 2-hole name declared with 3 argument sorts. Oracle warns + disables the op; a use no longer
*** parses and the session survives (the later `red a .` still computes). tnk loads it silently then panics
*** at the engine.rs arity assert on the first use.
fmod OPARITY is
  sort A .
  ops a b : -> A [ctor] .
  op _+_ : A A A -> A .
endfm
red in OPARITY : a + b .
red in OPARITY : a .

*** Case 2 (LAST): 3-hole name declared unary. Oracle warns + disables; tnk panics at module BUILD
*** in grammar/build.rs, so this module must come last or its pre-fix crash masks case 1.
fmod OPUNARY is
  sort A .
  op a : -> A [ctor] .
  op _;_;_ : A -> A .
endfm
red in OPUNARY : a .
